{
  "raw": {
    "https://franklinpierce.edu/paths": {
      "title": "Physician Assistant Pathways",
      "description": "Career Paths@Pierce - Franklin Pierce University Skip to main content Skip to footer content Search Franklin Pierce Menu Search Close Menu Visit Campus RaveNet Student Handbook CampusWeb Canvas Raven Athletics Giving What to Study What to Study All Programs Undergraduate Studies Graduate Studies Colleges & Centers Academic Catalog Online Courses Offered Application & Aid Application & Aid Net Price Calculator Loan Fee Calculator Get Started Visit Campus Tuition, Fees & Financial Aid Begin Your FAFSA Application After You're Admitted Parents & Families Request Information Apply Now Connect with Admissions Staff Pierce Promise New Hampshire Transfer Guarantee The Student Experience The Student Experience Visit Campus Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce International Student Services Parents & Families Campus Life Living on Campus Raven Recreation Student Handbook Student Wellness & Outreach Education Safety & Security Emergency Operations Student Affairs Office of Multicultural Student Services Student Consumer Information About Us About Us President Peter Eden Commencement 2026 Economic Impact Facts & Stats Leadership FPU Strategic Plan 2026-2029 Employers and Partnerships Alumni Resources Locations Faculty & Staff Directory News Pierce Magazine Academic Calendar Apply Now! Apply Now! On-Campus Undergraduate Application Online Undergraduate Application Graduate Application Search Career Paths@Pierce Home The Student Experience Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce Career Paths@Pierce Franklin Pierce University prepares students for career success. Through Career Paths@Pierce , all incoming FPU students are guaranteed multiple internships or other experiential\n                           learning opportunities. FPU also offers multiple direct pathways to graduate degrees\n                           to ensure smooth transitions between undergraduate and professional programs, and\n                           ultimately to a rewarding career. Career Education Our Career Center, is your hub to exploring interests, opportunities, enhancing your\n                                       professional profile, and launching—or revitalizing—your career. Career Education Success Stories Meet our Alumni who have gone on to start their careers. Meet Our Ravens! Graduate Pathways Explore the different pathways you can take toward an advanced degree and career in\n                           a variety of fields. Business Pathways Earn an undergraduate degree on campus—or completely online. Then pursue your Master of Business Administration (MBA) 100% online. Concentrations available in: Accounting , Finance , Healthcare Management , Leadership , Marketing and Sports Management . Clinical Mental Health Counseling Pathways After your complete your bachelor’s in any subject, continue onto the graduate-level Master’s in Clinical Mental Health Counseling program, offered online/hybrid. Popular with Psychology, Human Services, Criminal\n                                    Justice majors, and more. Doctor of Medicine Pathways Undergraduate study in Biology or Health Sciences at Franklin Pierce, Rindge, NH to the Doctor of Medicine (MD) graduate program at St. George’s University (SGU) School of Medicine , Grenada. Learn more about the SGU Pathway to the Doctor of Medicine degree. Education Pathways Franklin Pierce’s School of Education offers the Master of Education (M.Ed.) in Educational Leadership and the Master of\n                                    Education (M.Ed.) and Teacher Certification degrees.  Learn more about Pathways to a Career in Education . Environmental Science Pathways Graduate with a Bachelor's Degree in Environmental Science and Policy and complete your Master's in Environmental Studies in just 5 Years with the Franklin Pierce/Antioch 3+2 Program. Learn more about Your Pathway to a Career in Environmental Science . Healthcare Pathways Franklin Pierce University’s Bachelor of Science (BS) in Health Science degree program prepares students for graduate level studies with pathway options\n                                    including Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) , Master of Physician Assistant Studies (MPAS) , Master’s Entry Program in Nursing (MEPN) , and Doctor of Medicine (MD) . Law School Pathways If becoming a lawyer is your career goal, our Pre-Law Advising program is specifically designed to help you earn your bachelor’s degree while preparing\n                                       for law school. Nursing Pathways A Master of Science (MSN) is offered in Nursing Leadership , Nursing Education , Master's Entry Program in Nursing (MEPN) and the Master of Science in Nursing and Master of Business Administration Dual Degree. Download the Pathways to Nursing Guide or visit the Franklin Pierce University School of Nursing to learn more. Physical Therapy Pathways Launch your physical therapy career with our graduate-level program available at locations\n                                       in New Hampshire (full-time, on-site) or Arizona (full-time, hybrid). Doctor of Physical Therapy Graduate Program Doctor of Physical Therapy - Direct Entry Physician Assistant Pathways The Master of Physician Assistant Studies (MPAS) program is designed to train outstanding\n                                    PAs who are compassionate, patient-centered providers. Our MPAS programs are unique\n                                    in their emphasis on collaborative medicine and support of life-long learning. Master of Physician Assistant Studies (MPAS) New Hampshire-based, on-ground 27-month program Master of Physician Assistant Studies Hybrid Program (MPAS) Arizona-based, hybrid 24-month program Master of Physician Assistant Studies Hybrid Program (MPAS) Texas-based, hybrid 24-month program Master of Physician Assistant Studies – Direct Entry Graduate with a BS in Health Sciences offered in Rindge, NH, and continue to an MPAS graduate program offered in-person,\n                                    in Lebanon, NH or hybrid, in Goodyear, AZ. CONTACT The Lloyd & Helen Ament Astmann'69 Career Center (603) 899-1070 careercenter@franklinpierce.edu Monday - Friday, 8 am - 4:30 pm Request Info Visit Apply Make a Gift Locations lebanon, nh | map (603) 790-4059 goodyear, az | map (623) 518-2386 rindge, nh | map (603) 899-4000 manchester, nh | map (603) 647-3500 Round Rock, tx | map (512) 481-4010 Notice of Nondiscrimination Franklin Pierce University does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits\n                  sex discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates, as required\n                  by Title IX and its regulations, including in admission and employment.  Franklin\n                  Pierce University is an EO/AA/Vet/Disability employer. The Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights contact information is available\n                  at https://ocrcas.ed.gov/contact-ocr . Helpful Links VIRTUAL TOUR Employment Maps & Directions Calendar Bookstore Giving Alumni Resources Directory Library TITLE IX POLICY © 2026\n               \t\t\t\t\t\t\t Franklin Pierce University. All rights reserved. Website Accessibility Assistance Legal Profile Modal"
    },
