    "https://franklinpierce.edu/student-experience/support/career-services/index.html": {
      "title": "Career Education",
      "description": "Career Education - Franklin Pierce University Skip to main content Skip to footer content Search Franklin Pierce Menu Search Close Menu Visit Campus RaveNet Student Handbook CampusWeb Canvas Raven Athletics Giving What to Study What to Study All Programs Undergraduate Studies Graduate Studies Colleges & Centers Academic Catalog Online Courses Offered Application & Aid Application & Aid Net Price Calculator Loan Fee Calculator Get Started Visit Campus Tuition, Fees & Financial Aid Begin Your FAFSA Application After You're Admitted Parents & Families Request Information Apply Now Connect with Admissions Staff Pierce Promise New Hampshire Transfer Guarantee The Student Experience The Student Experience Visit Campus Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce International Student Services Parents & Families Campus Life Living on Campus Raven Recreation Student Handbook Student Wellness & Outreach Education Safety & Security Emergency Operations Student Affairs Office of Multicultural Student Services Student Consumer Information About Us About Us President Peter Eden Commencement 2026 Economic Impact Facts & Stats Leadership FPU Strategic Plan 2026-2029 Employers and Partnerships Alumni Resources Locations Faculty & Staff Directory News Pierce Magazine Academic Calendar Apply Now! Apply Now! On-Campus Undergraduate Application Online Undergraduate Application Graduate Application Search Career Education Home The Student Experience Support & Success Career Education Section Menu Student Career Education Alumni Career Education Employer Career Services Career Education Information for Parents Help a Raven Tech Tools Handshake Employer Guide Career Education Our Lloyd and Helen Ament Astmann ’69 Career Center, located in the Student Success\n                           Center, is your hub to exploring interests, opportunities, enhancing your professional\n                           profile, and launching—or revitalizing—your career. Start here if you’re a student\n                           or alumnus preparing to hit the job market, or an employer looking to hire Franklin\n                           Pierce talent. Current Students Find online internship/job postings, prepare for your job search, review the internship\n                                       process, and more. See Services for Students Pierce Alumni Advance your career, mentor a student, post a job, or find other ways to expand or\n                                       share your experience. See Services for Alumni Employers Recruit interns or employees, join an on-campus job fair, request referrals from our\n                                       staff, and explore other ways to connect. See Services for Employers More Career Services & Resources See other ways we help Franklin Pierce students imagine, chart, and realize their\n                              professional futures. Career Paths@Pierce Personalized Education Solutions for Every Student. Learn more Resources for Parents & Families Learn how you can help your student—and others—plan and launch their careers. Find Info for Parents U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics View the latest statistics regarding the job market. Learn more CONTACT The Lloyd & Helen Ament Astmann'69 Career Center (603) 899-1070 careercenter@franklinpierce.edu Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Request Info Visit Apply Make a Gift Locations lebanon, nh | map (603) 790-4059 goodyear, az | map (623) 518-2386 rindge, nh | map (603) 899-4000 manchester, nh | map (603) 647-3500 Round Rock, tx | map (512) 481-4010 Notice of Nondiscrimination Franklin Pierce University does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits\n                  sex discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates, as required\n                  by Title IX and its regulations, including in admission and employment.  Franklin\n                  Pierce University is an EO/AA/Vet/Disability employer. The Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights contact information is available\n                  at https://ocrcas.ed.gov/contact-ocr . Helpful Links VIRTUAL TOUR Employment Maps & Directions Calendar Bookstore Giving Alumni Resources Directory Library TITLE IX POLICY © 2026\n               \t\t\t\t\t\t\t Franklin Pierce University. All rights reserved. Website Accessibility Assistance Legal Profile Modal"
