    "https://franklinpierce.edu/student-experience/support/career-paths/success-stories.html": {
      "title": "Student Success Stories",
      "description": "Student Success Stories - Franklin Pierce University Skip to main content Skip to footer content Search Franklin Pierce Menu Search Close Menu Visit Campus RaveNet Student Handbook CampusWeb Canvas Raven Athletics Giving What to Study What to Study All Programs Undergraduate Studies Graduate Studies Colleges & Centers Academic Catalog Online Courses Offered Application & Aid Application & Aid Net Price Calculator Loan Fee Calculator Get Started Visit Campus Tuition, Fees & Financial Aid Begin Your FAFSA Application After You're Admitted Parents & Families Request Information Apply Now Connect with Admissions Staff Pierce Promise New Hampshire Transfer Guarantee The Student Experience The Student Experience Visit Campus Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce International Student Services Parents & Families Campus Life Living on Campus Raven Recreation Student Handbook Student Wellness & Outreach Education Safety & Security Emergency Operations Student Affairs Office of Multicultural Student Services Student Consumer Information About Us About Us President Peter Eden Commencement 2026 Economic Impact Facts & Stats Leadership FPU Strategic Plan 2026-2029 Employers and Partnerships Alumni Resources Locations Faculty & Staff Directory News Pierce Magazine Academic Calendar Apply Now! Apply Now! On-Campus Undergraduate Application Online Undergraduate Application Graduate Application Search Student Success Stories Home The Student Experience Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce Student Success Stories Section Menu Graduate Pathways Success Stories Career Education Meet Our Ravens! Hear from a few of our graduates about what Raven Nation means to them and their success. Learn how Franklin Pierce University's personalized approach to education can lead\n                           to an exciting and rewarding career. Alumni from a variety of academic programs were back on the Rindge Campus for the\n                           April 2026 Accepted Student & Preview Day to share with future Ravens and their families\n                           how their time at Pierce helped prepare them for rewarding careers. ASHLEY FEMINO ’25 “During my Junior and Senior year at Franklin Pierce, I was able to apply what I was\n                                    learning in my marketing and advertising classes through three internships with the\n                                    Keene SwampBats, FPU Athletics, and University Marketing. I knew I wanted a career\n                                    in sports marketing and, when I saw the opportunity at the Boston Red Sox, I said,\n                                    I’m ready for this!” Ashley was a Marketing Major and was the recipient of the Franklin\n                                    Pierce School of Business Wollmar Award. She is now a Partnership Activation Assistant\n                                    with the Boston Red Sox. AMELIA MAMONE MSN ’22 MEPN “Having a Master’s degree in Nursing made my job search feel effortless.I ended up\n                                    receiving an offer for every position that I had applied and interviewed for and having\n                                    the opportunity to pick from multiple units made me feel very comfortable with my\n                                    decision. I recently started my career on a Cardiology unit at Albany Medical Center\n                                    in New York. I feel extremely grateful to have been a part of such an amazing program,\n                                    that filled my future with countless opportunities. I would encourage anyone who is\n                                    looking to go into the nursing field to apply to the MEPN program and pave your future\n                                    for nothing but success!” Amelia completed the Master’s Entry Program in Nursing (MEPN),\n                                    achieving her Masters of Science in Nursing and a Health Administration Graduate Certificate.\n                                    She is now with Albany Medical Center, Cardiology Dept., Albany, NY. BRENDAN CERONE ’22 “One of the biggest reasons I chose FPU was the Sports Media program. I always knew\n                                    I wanted to work in the sports industry and being able to study media practices for\n                                    sports specifically ended up helping tremendously when applying for my current job.\n                                    I was able to grow as a videographer and editor through my studies and working for\n                                    FPU Athletic Communications, Ravens Sports Network, and the Marlin Fitzwater Center\n                                    for Communication. With my Digital Media Design minor, I learned the basics of social\n                                    media management and content creation, as well as website building. I absolutely loved\n                                    my time at FPU, and I’m now fulfilling my dream of working full time in the sports\n                                    media industry because of everything I learned there.” Brendan was a Sports Media\n                                    Major and a Digital Media Design Minor. He is now a Digital Media Specialist for the\n                                    Worcester Railers Professional Hockey Club. Alison Jankowski ’22 “My studies at Franklin Pierce helped me to choose my career path in Digital Marketing.\n                                    When I think of FPU, I appreciate the fact that I was never just a number there. Professors\n                                    knew me by name, truly cared about me as a person and were invested as much as I was\n                                    in my success. There truly is no place like FPU!” Alison was a Digital Media Design\n                                    and Communications Major and an Advertising Minor, and is now a Graduate Student. NATALIE PATRUNO ’22 “Franklin Pierce taught me to get out of my comfort zone and try new things, to be\n                                    a leader, work hard, and support others. These qualities are what have made such an\n                                    important impact on my career. Because of Franklin Pierce, I have the confidence to\n                                    train new staff, give them support and guide them, and encourage them. Franklin Pierce\n                                    also taught me to keep going until I reach the top which is why I continued on to\n                                    graduate school.” Natalie was a Psychology Major and a Forensic Psychology Minor.\n                                    Senior Registered Behavior Technician, Autism Care Partners. LEONARD SCHWARTZ ’22 “Throughout my time at Franklin Pierce University, Professors Mary Kelly and Melinda\n                                    Jette really shaped my academic journey. They poured countless hours into one-on-one\n                                    meetings, fine-tuning my writing skills, and helping me grasp complex content. But\n                                    it did not stop there—they were like career coaches, too, guiding me through potential\n                                    paths and even pitching in with lesson plans during my student teaching at Jaffrey-Rindge\n                                    Middle School. History courses weren't just challenging; they were eye-opening, giving\n                                    me the analytical skills and historical content for my teaching career and graduate\n                                    school. Now, as I'm pursuing a Masters, their mentorship is still paying off big time,\n                                    helping me navigate the rigors of graduate-level coursework and research.” Leonard\n                                    Double Majored in Education and History. He is now a Professor of IB Business Management\n                                    and World History at New Hampton School. ELIZABETH JURGILEWICZ ’20 “At Franklin Pierce, I was challenged through intensive independent studies and practicums,\n                                    including archaeological field school and my public history internship. Through my\n                                    internship at the Rindge Historical Society, I was able to join the Board of Directors,\n                                    where I remain today. The hands-on experience within the community prepared me for\n                                    working in the field. The smaller class sizes and individualized attention played\n                                    a large role in shaping my career path.”Elizabeth was a History Major. She is now\n                                    a Program Specialist, with the State of New Hampshire Department of Natural and Cultural\n                                    Resources Division of Parks and Recreation, Bureau of Historic Site . BAILEY CLAPP ’19,’21, MS “During my time at Franklin Pierce, I made it a point to get involved with as many\n                                    extracurriculars as I could. I believe that had an extremely positive impact on my\n                                    confidence and professionalism as I transitioned to a full-time employment opportunity.\n                                    In both my undergraduate and graduate programs, I benefited from working with the\n                                    same professors throughout my entire higher education career, as I was able to connect\n                                    with them on a more personal level. I got hands-on experience during my internship\n                                    at C&S Wholesale Grocers, and I was able to take on projects as well as cross train\n                                    with the full-time staff. I still work at C&S today!” Bailey studied Accounting and\n                                    Finance as an undergrad and then achieved her Master of Science in Accounting. She\n                                    is now a Financial Analyst, C&S Wholesale Grocers. Justin Langhill '13 “Franklin Pierce will always be the place where I discovered myself—not just academically,\n                                    but personally and professionally. It’s where I learned that leadership isn’t about\n                                    titles; it’s about service, persistence, and the courage to raise a hand when others\n                                    might not. What made my experience so special was the chance to be part of something\n                                    new, while also being surrounded by a tight-knit community that gave me the freedom\n                                    to try—even when I didn’t fully believe in myself. To me, Franklin Pierce represents\n                                    opportunity, growth, and the beginning of a lifelong journey of leadership—one that\n                                    I now walk out with both confidence and faith.”Justin was a Marketing Major. He is\n                                    now a Professional Golf Performance Coach. Bailey Clapp '19 '21 A Franklin Pierce University graduate, Bailey Clapp, '19, '21, talks about her experience\n                                       on campus and her success at C&S Wholesale Grocers as a Financial Analyst. Nidhi Patel '17, '19 Coming to America from India in search of a better education, Nidhi Patel '17, '19,\n                                       found her opportunity at Franklin Pierce University where she earned a BS in Health\n                                       Sciences, and then continued on to get her MBA in Health Administration. Jeremy Blydenburgh-Cote '20 Jeremy Blydenburgh-Cote '20 shares how an internship opportunity led him to his current\n                                       role. John Massaro BA '18, MSW'23 John Massaro '18 talks about his close connections with faculty members inspired his\n                                       career path. Hear from Abbie Trombly '18 about how her time at Franklin Pierce and her internship\n                           helped prepare her for a rewarding career. CONTACT the admissions team UNDERGRADUATE ADMISSIONS (800) 437-0048 admissions@franklinpierce.edu Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Online Admissions (800) 325-1090 FPUonline@franklinpierce.edu Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.- 4:30 p.m. Apply Now Request Info Visit Apply Make a Gift Locations lebanon, nh | map (603) 790-4059 goodyear, az | map (623) 518-2386 rindge, nh | map (603) 899-4000 manchester, nh | map (603) 647-3500 Round Rock, tx | map (512) 481-4010 Notice of Nondiscrimination Franklin Pierce University does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits\n                  sex discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates, as required\n                  by Title IX and its regulations, including in admission and employment.  Franklin\n                  Pierce University is an EO/AA/Vet/Disability employer. The Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights contact information is available\n                  at https://ocrcas.ed.gov/contact-ocr . Helpful Links VIRTUAL TOUR Employment Maps & Directions Calendar Bookstore Giving Alumni Resources Directory Library TITLE IX POLICY © 2026\n               \t\t\t\t\t\t\t Franklin Pierce University. All rights reserved. Website Accessibility Assistance Legal Video Modal Profile Modal"
    },
    "https://franklinpierce.edu/academics/programs/education-pathways.html": {
      "title": "Your Pathway to an Education Career",
      "description": "Your Pathway to a Career in Education  - Franklin Pierce University Skip to main content Skip to footer content Search Franklin Pierce Menu Search Close Menu Visit Campus RaveNet Student Handbook CampusWeb Canvas Raven Athletics Giving What to Study What to Study All Programs Undergraduate Studies Graduate Studies Colleges & Centers Academic Catalog Online Courses Offered Application & Aid Application & Aid Net Price Calculator Loan Fee Calculator Get Started Visit Campus Tuition, Fees & Financial Aid Begin Your FAFSA Application After You're Admitted Parents & Families Request Information Apply Now Connect with Admissions Staff Pierce Promise New Hampshire Transfer Guarantee The Student Experience The Student Experience Visit Campus Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce International Student Services Parents & Families Campus Life Living on Campus Raven Recreation Student Handbook Student Wellness & Outreach Education Safety & Security Emergency Operations Student Affairs Office of Multicultural Student Services Student Consumer Information About Us About Us President Peter Eden Commencement 2026 Economic Impact Facts & Stats Leadership FPU Strategic Plan 2026-2029 Employers and Partnerships Alumni Resources Locations Faculty & Staff Directory News Pierce Magazine Academic Calendar Apply Now! Apply Now! On-Campus Undergraduate Application Online Undergraduate Application Graduate Application Search Your Pathway to an Education Career Home What to Study All Programs Your Pathway to Education Information Request Find Your Path to a Rewarding Career in Education Earn your Master of Education (M.Ed) in Educational Leadership or your Teacher Certification.\n                           Teacher certification is offered locally within proximity of Rindge, NH. Take courses\n                           in your chosen content area, and study emerging trends in education. Fill out the form below to request information about Franklin Pierce’s School of Education. . CONTACT Us School of Education Sonya Prince Associate Director, School of Education (603) 899-1148 Program Sheets Elementary Education Secondary Education Special Education Master's in Educational Leadership Master's in Education and Teacher Certification Apply Now Request Info Visit Apply Make a Gift Locations lebanon, nh | map (603) 790-4059 goodyear, az | map (623) 518-2386 rindge, nh | map (603) 899-4000 manchester, nh | map (603) 647-3500 Round Rock, tx | map (512) 481-4010 Notice of Nondiscrimination Franklin Pierce University does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits\n                  sex discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates, as required\n                  by Title IX and its regulations, including in admission and employment.  Franklin\n                  Pierce University is an EO/AA/Vet/Disability employer. The Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights contact information is available\n                  at https://ocrcas.ed.gov/contact-ocr . Helpful Links VIRTUAL TOUR Employment Maps & Directions Calendar Bookstore Giving Alumni Resources Directory Library TITLE IX POLICY © 2026\n               \t\t\t\t\t\t\t Franklin Pierce University. All rights reserved. Website Accessibility Assistance Legal Profile Modal"
    },
    "https://franklinpierce.edu/academics/programs/environmental-science-pathway.html": {
      "title": "Environmental Sciences Pathways Program",
      "description": "Environmental Sciences Pathways Program - Franklin Pierce University Skip to main content Skip to footer content Search Franklin Pierce Menu Search Close Menu Visit Campus RaveNet Student Handbook CampusWeb Canvas Raven Athletics Giving What to Study What to Study All Programs Undergraduate Studies Graduate Studies Colleges & Centers Academic Catalog Online Courses Offered Application & Aid Application & Aid Net Price Calculator Loan Fee Calculator Get Started Visit Campus Tuition, Fees & Financial Aid Begin Your FAFSA Application After You're Admitted Parents & Families Request Information Apply Now Connect with Admissions Staff Pierce Promise New Hampshire Transfer Guarantee The Student Experience The Student Experience Visit Campus Support & Success Career Paths@Pierce International Student Services Parents & Families Campus Life Living on Campus Raven Recreation Student Handbook Student Wellness & Outreach Education Safety & Security Emergency Operations Student Affairs Office of Multicultural Student Services Student Consumer Information About Us About Us President Peter Eden Commencement 2026 Economic Impact Facts & Stats Leadership FPU Strategic Plan 2026-2029 Employers and Partnerships Alumni Resources Locations Faculty & Staff Directory News Pierce Magazine Academic Calendar Apply Now! Apply Now! On-Campus Undergraduate Application Online Undergraduate Application Graduate Application Search Environmental Sciences Pathways Program Home What to Study All Programs Environmental Sciences Pathways Program Section Menu Accounting Advertising Anthropology Biology Business Chemistry Communications Criminal Justice Education Environmental Science Emergency Medical Services General Studies Global Citizenship Graphic and Digital Communication Documentary Studies Finance Healthcare Administration Health Practice Management Health Science History Human Resources Management Human Services Integrated Studies Intelligence Security Studies Leadership Management Marketing Music Nursing Paralegal Philosophy Physical Therapy Physician Assistant Political Science Psychology Public Health Public Relations SGU Pathway Sociology Spanish Sports Media Sports Management Study Abroad Visual Arts Women in Leadership English Mathematical Modeling Nutrition Pre-Medicine Pre-Veterinary Medicine Physician Assistant (MPAS) Physical Therapy Health Science Nursing Energy & Sustainability Environmental Studies / Sciences Master's 3+2 Pathway Master of Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program Master of Business Administration (MBA) Environmental Sciences | Environmental Studies 3+2 Graduate with a Bachelor's Degree and Master's Degree in 5 Years with the Antioch\n                           3+2 Program. Explore the 3+2 Environmental Science/Studies Degree to Master's Pathway Program to\n                        complete a master's degree in just five years. Spend your first three years in the\n                        Environmental Science or Environmental Studies undergraduate degree at Franklin Pierce,\n                        completing all of your General and Liberal Education courses, and most of your major\n                        courses. Then enter into the two-year Master of Science program at Antioch University,\n                        selecting either Environmental Studies or Resource, Management, and Conservation as\n                        your program of study. Work through a collaborative teaching model to explore this relevant and expanding\n                        field. Senior year coursework (year 4) will be credited from both universities toward\n                        both degrees. HOW DO I GET INTO THE pathway PROGRAM? Completion of all General Education requirements at FPU Be on track to complete at least 96 credits at FPU at the conclusion of your junior\n                                    year Minimum 3.0 GPA in the major at FPU at the conclusion of the fall semester of your\n                                    junior year Two letters of recommendation from FPU faculty; at least one from a faculty associated\n                                    with the Environmental Science or Environmental Studies majors. Interview with the relevant AUNE Concentration Director M.S. in Environmental Studies Learn more about Antioch's graduate program in Environmental Studies. CONTACT our admissions team UNDERGRADUATE ADMISSIONS (800) 437-0048 admissions@franklinpierce.edu Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.-4:30 p.m. graduate/online Admissions (800) 325-1090 FPUonline@franklinpierce.edu Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.- 4:30 p.m. Apply Now Request Info Visit Apply Make a Gift Locations lebanon, nh | map (603) 790-4059 goodyear, az | map (623) 518-2386 rindge, nh | map (603) 899-4000 manchester, nh | map (603) 647-3500 Round Rock, tx | map (512) 481-4010 Notice of Nondiscrimination Franklin Pierce University does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits\n                  sex discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates, as required\n                  by Title IX and its regulations, including in admission and employment.  Franklin\n                  Pierce University is an EO/AA/Vet/Disability employer. The Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights contact information is available\n                  at https://ocrcas.ed.gov/contact-ocr . Helpful Links VIRTUAL TOUR Employment Maps & Directions Calendar Bookstore Giving Alumni Resources Directory Library TITLE IX POLICY © 2026\n               \t\t\t\t\t\t\t Franklin Pierce University. All rights reserved. Website Accessibility Assistance Legal Profile Modal"
    },
